"""A-001 — the general plan notes, on their own sheet.

   They were on A-101 and A-102 when the set was 22 x 34 portrait: 17.7 inches of a
   32.5-inch sheet. On a 16.5-inch drawing area they no longer fit beside a plan, so
   they moved here and the plan sheets carry a cross-reference. That is also what let
   the plans stay at 1/4" = 1'-0" rather than dropping a scale step.

   Set in TWO COLUMNS. The lines are lifted verbatim from the sheets they replaced,
   so the line COUNT is fixed and only the setting can give."""
