# ============================= A-001 PLAN NOTES =============================
# The notes are not a document that happens to quote the drawings — they are built
# from the same values the drawings are, which is why this list lives beside the
# sheet that prints it and not in a data file. Forty-odd derived figures appear in
# it: the glazing percentages, the stair run, the terminations. Mechanical, electrical
# and structural detail is not repeated here: the note points to its home sheet.
# General plan notes — drawn on A-001, referenced from every plan sheet.

def _wc_side():
    """The clearance note 11a quotes: the smaller of the two the Building 1 plans
       dimension at the pan.

       Not a number typed in the note. The citation and both minimums beside it come
       from src/clearances.py and this comes from wc_clearances(), which is the same
       measurement A-101 and A-102 draw -- so the note, the dimension on the sheet and
       the check that passes or fails the build are three readings of one figure. RCO
       307.1 used to live only in prose, in a symbol docstring that said it was checked
       in build.py when nothing was."""
    return min(min(m['cl']-m['lo'], m['hi']-m['cl'])
               for lab, r, po, fu in CL.project_plans() if lab.startswith('BUILDING 1')
               for m in wc_clearances(r, po, fu, BOARD))


